    "marketing.terms.s1.title": "1. About SoundBloom",
    "marketing.terms.s1.body": "SoundBloom is a web music platform that lets you discover and stream tracks from integrated catalogs (including Jamendo and iTunes APIs), save favorites to your library, and—if you register as an artist—upload your own original music subject to moderation.",
    "marketing.terms.s2.title": "2. Eligibility and accounts",
    "marketing.terms.s2.body": "You must be at least 13 years old (or the minimum age required in your country) to use SoundBloom. You are responsible for keeping your login credentials confidential and for all activity under your account. Provide accurate email and profile information.",
    "marketing.terms.s3.title": "3. Personal use of the service",
    "marketing.terms.s3.body": "SoundBloom is intended for personal, non-commercial listening unless otherwise stated. You may like tracks, save albums, genres, and playlists to your library. You may not scrape, bulk-download, or redistribute catalog content outside the app without permission from rights holders.",
    "marketing.terms.s4.title": "4. Artist profiles and uploads",
    "marketing.terms.s4.body": "To upload music you must complete artist registration with truthful information (name, genre, location, PRO membership where applicable). You warrant that you own or control rights to uploaded audio, lyrics, and artwork. Uploaded tracks enter moderation and may be approved, rejected, or removed. You grant SoundBloom a non-exclusive license to host, stream, and display your content within the platform.",
    "marketing.terms.s5.title": "5. Content standards",
    "marketing.terms.s5.body": "You may not upload or share content that infringes copyright, promotes violence or hatred, contains illegal material, malware, or deceptive metadata. Cover art must meet stated technical requirements. Explicit lyrics must be marked accordingly during upload.",
    "marketing.terms.s6.title": "6. Licenses you choose for your tracks",
    "marketing.terms.s6.body": "During upload you select licensing options (commercial use, derivative works). You are responsible for ensuring your choices reflect your actual rights and intentions. SoundBloom displays these settings to listeners where applicable but does not provide legal advice.",
